    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17465" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Făbĕrĭus</span></b> ,
		a, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a Roman gens</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				12, 25, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">15, 13, 3</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Făbĕrĭānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Faberius</i> (a debtor of Cicero): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">negotium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 13, 31, 1</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 13, 29, 3</span></i>; 12, 31,
			2.</div>
